            </apex:form>

            <hr class="gfg2-section-rule" />

            <!-- Static workbook intro content -->
            <p class="gfg2-body">
                The objective of this workbook is to give the Federal Employee a working
                knowledge of their current core benefits. It is not intended to offer tax
                or investing advice. Understanding how the federal retirement system works
                will offer you invaluable insight and the ability to make an informed
                decision when the time comes to plan for your retirement. Your retirement
                income is based on the system you are employed under, either CSRS, CSRS
                Offset, or FERS. While it is important to understand how this works, it is
                equally important to understand your other core benefits, what they are,
                how they affect your income during your working years, and how to maximize
                your pension into retirement.
            </p>

            <h2 class="gfg2-h2">
                The first steps in developing a financial strategy involve understanding:
            </h2>
            <ul class="gfg2-cols">
                <li>What you have</li>
                <li>What you want</li>
                <li>What your costs will be</li>
                <li>What you need</li>
                <li>What your income will be</li>
                <li>What your options are</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="gfg2-h2">
                During this review we will cover the following core benefits that apply to you:
            </h2>
            <ul class="gfg2-cols">
                <li>Your Federal Retirement System</li>
                <li>Retirement Annuity</li>
                <li>FERS Supplement Annuity</li>
                <li>Thrift Savings Plan</li>
                <li>Social Security Annuity</li>
                <li>Federal Employee Group Life Insurance</li>
                <li>Survivor Benefits Plan</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script type="text/javascript">
        // Retirement System: FERS and Special Groups are mutually exclusive and
        // complementary — exactly one is selected, mirroring the legacy
        // GPIS_Federal_Workbook save() logic (FERS__c and Special_Group_Member__c
        // are always set opposite). Invoked inline from each checkbox's onchange
        // BEFORE gfg2Save(), so the other box is toggled before the auto-save
        // posts the form.
        function gfg2RetSys(clicked) {
            if (!clicked) { return; }
            var group = document.getElementById('gfg2-retsys-group');
            if (!group) { return; }
            var inputs = group.getElementsByTagName('input');
            for (var i = 0; i < inputs.length; i++) {
                if (inputs[i].type === 'checkbox' && inputs[i] !== clicked) {
                    inputs[i].checked = !clicked.checked;
                }
            }
        }
    </script>
</apex:page>
